# Matter pages: licensing, debt recovery (business to business only). No em dashes.
from matters_property import m

LICENSING = [
    m('premises-licence-applications', 'Premises licence applications', 'Applying for a new premises licence to sell alcohol or provide entertainment.',
      ['To sell alcohol, provide regulated entertainment or late night food, premises usually need a premises licence from the local council under the Licensing Act 2003. The application includes an operating schedule, plans and notices.',
       'A licensing solicitor will prepare the application, talk to the police and council before it goes in and represent you at a hearing if there are objections.'],
      ['Preparing the application and operating schedule', 'Plans and public notices', 'Pre-application talks with the police and council', 'Dealing with representations', 'Hearings before the licensing committee'],
      ['The premises address', 'What you want to do and your hours', 'Your opening date', 'Who will be the designated premises supervisor'],
      [('How long does a new licence take?', 'There is a consultation period after the application, and longer if there is a hearing. Allow plenty of time before opening.'),
       ('What happens if someone objects?', 'The council holds a hearing. A solicitor can negotiate conditions beforehand and represent you.'),
       ('Do I need a personal licence too?', 'Premises selling alcohol need a designated premises supervisor with a personal licence.')],
      'New licence applications come from businesses with an opening date, which makes them motivated clients.'),
    m('licence-variations', 'Licence variations', 'Changing hours, layout or activities on an existing licence.',
      ['If you want to extend your hours, change the layout, add activities or remove conditions, you will usually need to vary your premises licence. Small changes can sometimes use a quicker minor variation.',
       'A solicitor will advise on the right type of application, prepare it and deal with any objections.'],
      ['Full and minor variations', 'Extending hours', 'Changing plans and layout', 'Removing or amending conditions', 'Hearings if needed'],
      ['Your current licence', 'What you want to change', 'Any deadline'],
      [('What is a minor variation?', 'A simpler process for changes that won’t affect the licensing objectives.'),
       ('Can I extend my hours?', 'You can apply. Residents and authorities may object.'),
       ('How long does it take?', 'It depends on the type of variation and whether there are objections.')],
      'Variation enquiries come from established operators who often need ongoing licensing support.'),
    m('transfers-and-dps', 'Transfers and DPS changes', 'Transferring a licence or changing the designated premises supervisor.',
      ['When a business is bought or the operator changes, the premises licence needs to be transferred. When a manager leaves, the designated premises supervisor needs to be changed. Both can usually take effect quickly if done correctly.',
       'A solicitor will prepare the applications and deal with any police objection.'],
      ['Premises licence transfers', 'Changing the designated premises supervisor', 'Licensing work on a business sale', 'Dealing with police objections'],
      ['The current licence', 'Details of the new holder or DPS', 'Any sale completion date'],
      [('Can I trade while a transfer is processed?', 'Often yes, if the application asks for immediate effect.'),
       ('Does a new DPS need a personal licence?', 'Yes.'),
       ('Can the police object?', 'Yes, in exceptional circumstances. A solicitor can represent you.')],
      'Transfers are often part of a business purchase, alongside commercial property and corporate work.'),
    m('licence-reviews', 'Licence reviews and hearings', 'Representation when your premises licence is under review.',
      ['A review can be called by the police, the council, residents or other responsible authorities. The committee can add conditions, suspend the licence or revoke it.',
       'Reviews are serious and time-sensitive. A licensing solicitor will look at the evidence, talk to the authorities and represent you at the hearing.'],
      ['Responding to a review application', 'Negotiating conditions with the authorities', 'Preparing evidence', 'Representation at the hearing', 'Appeals'],
      ['The review application', 'The hearing date', 'Your current licence and any incident details'],
      [('Can my licence be revoked?', 'Yes. That is why expert representation is important.'),
       ('Can I keep trading during a review?', 'Usually, unless there has been a summary review with interim steps.'),
       ('Can I appeal?', 'Yes, to the magistrates’ court, within a time limit.')],
      'Review enquiries are urgent and high stakes for the business, which makes them some of the most valuable licensing work.'),
    m('personal-licences', 'Personal licences', 'Applying for or defending a personal licence.',
      ['A personal licence allows someone to authorise alcohol sales. Holders need to tell the council about relevant convictions, and a licence can be suspended or revoked.',
       'A solicitor can help with applications where there are convictions and represent you if the council considers action against your licence.'],
      ['Applications with relevant convictions', 'Responding to police objections', 'Hearings about suspension or revocation', 'Advice on notification duties'],
      ['Your licence or application details', 'Details of any convictions', 'Any letters from the council'],
      [('Do convictions stop me getting a licence?', 'Not always. The police can object, and the council decides.'),
       ('Can my licence be taken away?', 'It can be suspended or revoked in some circumstances.'),
       ('Do I need to tell the council about a conviction?', 'Personal licence holders have duties to notify. Get advice.')],
      'Personal licence matters are smaller instructions that often come from larger operators.'),
    m('taxi-and-private-hire-licences', 'Taxi and private hire licences', 'Help for drivers and operators with council licences.',
      ['Taxi and private hire drivers, vehicles and operators are licensed by local councils. Licences can be refused, suspended or revoked, sometimes quickly, which can stop a driver working.',
       'A licensing solicitor will help with applications, respond to council action and represent drivers at hearings and appeals.'],
      ['Driver, vehicle and operator applications', 'Responding to complaints and suspensions', 'Hearings before the licensing committee', 'Appeals to the magistrates’ court'],
      ['Your licence details', 'Any letter from the council', 'The hearing date, if any'],
      [('Can my licence be suspended straight away?', 'In some cases, yes. Get advice quickly.'),
       ('Can I appeal a revocation?', 'Usually, to the magistrates’ court within a time limit.'),
       ('Do you help operators?', 'Yes, we can introduce operators as well as drivers.')],
      'Driver licensing enquiries are urgent because the client’s income depends on the outcome.'),
]

DEBT = [
    m('unpaid-invoices', 'Unpaid invoices', 'Recovering money owed to your business by another business.',
      ['If a customer hasn’t paid, a solicitor’s letter is often enough to get the money moving. If not, they can take court action and enforce any judgment.',
       'A debt recovery solicitor will check your contract and invoices, advise on the best route and act quickly. Leaflegal only introduces businesses chasing debts owed by other businesses.'],
      ['Reviewing contracts and invoices', 'Letters before action', 'Court claims', 'Statutory demands and insolvency routes', 'Enforcement'],
      ['Copies of the invoices and contract or terms', 'Correspondence with the customer', 'The customer’s company details', 'Whether the debt is disputed'],
      [('Can I recover my legal costs?', 'Some costs can be recovered, and fixed compensation and interest may be claimed under late payment law. A solicitor will explain.'),
       ('What if the debt is disputed?', 'The solicitor will advise on the strength of the dispute and the right route.'),
       ('Do you help with consumer debts?', 'No. We only introduce businesses recovering debts from other businesses.')],
      'Business debt clients want a firm that acts quickly and charges clearly, and often have more than one debt.'),
    m('letters-before-action', 'Letters before action', 'A formal demand before court proceedings.',
      ['A letter before action tells the debtor what is owed, why, and that court proceedings will follow if they don’t pay. Many debts are paid at this stage.',
       'A solicitor will make sure the letter is correct, includes interest and compensation where appropriate, and complies with any pre-action requirements.'],
      ['Drafting and sending the letter', 'Calculating interest and compensation', 'Pre-action requirements', 'Negotiating payment plans', 'Next steps if the debt isn’t paid'],
      ['Invoices and contract terms', 'The debtor’s details', 'Previous reminders'],
      [('Is a solicitor’s letter more effective?', 'It often is, because it shows you are prepared to go to court.'),
       ('How long does the debtor have to respond?', 'It depends on who the debtor is. The solicitor will set the right deadline.'),
       ('Can I add interest?', 'Often, under your contract or late payment law.')],
      'Letter before action work is quick, low-friction and often leads to further instructions.'),
    m('court-claims', 'Court claims for debts', 'Issuing a claim in the County Court or High Court.',
      ['If a debt isn’t paid, a solicitor can issue a court claim. Many undefended claims end in a default judgment quickly. Defended claims go through the court process.',
       'The solicitor will choose the right court and procedure, handle the claim and advise on enforcement.'],
      ['Issuing claims', 'Default judgments', 'Defended claims', 'Settlement negotiations', 'Enforcement after judgment'],
      ['Invoices, contract and correspondence', 'The letter before action', 'The debtor’s details'],
      [('How long does a claim take?', 'Undefended claims can be quick. Defended claims take longer.'),
       ('What if the debtor ignores the claim?', 'You can usually ask for judgment in default.'),
       ('What happens after judgment?', 'If the debtor still doesn’t pay, there are several enforcement options.')],
      'Court claims are chargeable, structured work for commercial litigation teams.'),
    m('statutory-demands', 'Statutory demands', 'A formal demand that can lead to winding up or bankruptcy.',
      ['A statutory demand is a formal demand for payment of an undisputed debt. For a company debt of more than £750, failing to pay or respond within 21 days can allow a creditor to petition to wind the company up.',
       'Statutory demands are powerful but should only be used for undisputed debts. A solicitor will advise whether it is the right tool.'],
      ['Advising whether a statutory demand is suitable', 'Preparing and serving the demand', 'Next steps after 21 days', 'Responding to an application to set aside'],
      ['Invoices and proof the debt is undisputed', 'The debtor’s details', 'Correspondence'],
      [('Can I use a statutory demand for a disputed debt?', 'It is risky and can lead to costs. Get advice first.'),
       ('What happens after 21 days?', 'You may be able to present a winding up or bankruptcy petition.'),
       ('Is it the same for sole traders?', 'Bankruptcy has different thresholds and rules. A solicitor will explain.')],
      'Statutory demand enquiries come from creditors ready to apply pressure, a clear instruction.'),
    m('winding-up-petitions', 'Winding up petitions', 'Petitioning to wind up a company that won’t pay.',
      ['A winding up petition asks the court to put a company into compulsory liquidation because it can’t pay its debts. It is often used where a statutory demand or judgment has gone unpaid.',
       'It is a serious step for both sides. A solicitor will advise whether it is right for your debt and handle the petition.'],
      ['Advising on whether to petition', 'Preparing and presenting the petition', 'Advertising and hearings', 'Negotiating settlement', 'Working with insolvency practitioners'],
      ['Details of the debt and any judgment or statutory demand', 'The company’s details'],
      [('Will I get paid if the company is wound up?', 'Not necessarily. Creditors share what is left. Many debtors pay before the hearing.'),
       ('Is it expensive?', 'There are court fees and a deposit. The solicitor will explain the costs.'),
       ('Can the company stop the petition?', 'It can pay, settle or dispute the debt.')],
      'Winding up work is specialist insolvency litigation with substantial fees.'),
    m('enforcement', 'Enforcing a judgment', 'Getting paid after you win in court.',
      ['A judgment doesn’t always mean payment. If the debtor still doesn’t pay, there are several ways to enforce, including enforcement agents, charging orders over property and third party debt orders.',
       'A solicitor will find out what the debtor owns and choose the method most likely to work.'],
      ['Investigating the debtor’s assets', 'Writs and warrants of control', 'Charging orders', 'Third party debt orders', 'Orders to obtain information'],
      ['Your judgment', 'What you know about the debtor’s assets', 'Payments received so far'],
      [('Which enforcement method is best?', 'It depends on the debtor’s assets. A solicitor will advise.'),
       ('Can I enforce against a company’s property?', 'A charging order can secure the debt against property.'),
       ('How long is a judgment valid?', 'Different rules apply to different enforcement methods. Act promptly.')],
      'Enforcement enquiries come from clients who already have a judgment and want results.'),
    m('late-payment-interest', 'Late payment interest and compensation', 'Claiming statutory interest and compensation on late invoices.',
      ['Under the Late Payment of Commercial Debts (Interest) Act 1998, businesses can usually claim interest at 8% above the Bank of England base rate on late business invoices, plus fixed compensation, unless their contract says otherwise.',
       'A solicitor will calculate what you can claim and include it in demands and court claims.'],
      ['Calculating statutory interest', 'Fixed compensation per invoice', 'Reasonable recovery costs', 'Including interest in claims'],
      ['Your invoices and payment terms', 'Your contract terms on interest'],
      [('Can I claim interest on every late invoice?', 'Usually, between businesses, unless your contract sets a different rate.'),
       ('What compensation can I add?', 'A fixed sum per invoice depending on its size, plus reasonable recovery costs in some cases.'),
       ('Does it apply to consumers?', 'No. It applies to business to business debts.')],
      'Late payment claims add value to every debt recovery instruction.'),
]
